        "committer": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-26 05:19:26.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20611 llapi: skip a scanned inode reused mid-read",
        "message": "LU-20611 llapi: skip a scanned inode reused mid-read\n\nlfs find --target, --local and --fsname read targets in service.  A\nscan reads an inode's external xattr block after the inode, so the\ninode can be freed and reused by another file in between, and the\nrecord gets that file's xattrs.\n\nAfter reading an external block, scan_inode_unchanged() reads the\ninode again and skips the object if its generation or xattr block\nchanged.  It uses pread() because ext2fs_read_inode() would answer\nfrom its inode cache.  Only objects with an external xattr block pay\nfor it.  Also set \"cache=off\" on the worker's io channel, so a cached\nxattr block that has since been given to another file is not read.\n\nFixes: 552b4546c690 (\"LU-20606 llapi: scan an ldiskfs target directly\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Id47a5315269e76029e19c9ce32dd50a5073cdb59\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
